<p>Three segments, and for each we separate need, want and demand, as in the course. A teacher needs teaching material, wants a bilingual poster, and the demand is a nine-euro A3 poster or a school pack. Merchandise is a buyer’s market, so we compete on value and trust, not price. And it is social marketing: every item carries a behaviour.</p>
